   "description": "This edition of Luke Howard’s CLIMATE OF LONDON has been produced by the\r\nInternational Association for Urban Climate (IAUC). While Howard is best known for his work on\r\nclouds1, he was also the first to recognise the effect that urban areas have on local climate. Much of\r\nhis studies on climate, including his description, analysis and observations, are contained in CLIMATE ,\r\nwhich can reasonably claim to be the first textbook on climatology. Despite its title, the majority of\r\nthe book is concerned with weather and climate in general, rather than that of the London\r\nmetropolis. Nevertheless, one hundred and thirty-two years after its publication, Chandler dedicated\r\nhis study of the spatial and temporal character of metropolis’ climate to Luke Howard (1772-1864),\r\nwhom he described as the pioneer of urban climatic studies."
  },
